# Supabase — P0-A auth, P0-B provenance-tagged data, Task 12 offline bundle storage
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Mapbox — Map-Driven Exploration pillar
NEXT_PUBLIC_MAPBOX_TOKEN=

# Task 16 — "Claim this listing" contact address
# (src/components/lds/claim-listing.tsx). The address a dive-shop owner
# emails to ask for their LDS listing to be promoted COMMUNITY -> VERIFIED.
# That promotion is a manual, founder-run SQL update (supabase/README.md: no
# moderator role is modeled, promotion needs the service-role key), so this
# is the entire "backend" of the claim process by design.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ on purpose — it's rendered into a mailto: link in the browser
# and is not a secret. Leave it unset and the UI degrades honestly: the
# claim notice still explains the process but shows no dead mailto link.
# MUST be set to a real, monitored address before this ships to real shop
# owners; a published inbox (not a personal one) is the better choice, since
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ values are inlined into the client bundle and scrapeable.
NEXT_PUBLIC_LDS_CLAIM_EMAIL=

# Offline bundle signing (Task 12 / T12.2, src/lib/offline/bundle-signing.ts)
# — server-only secret used to HMAC-sign offline bundle manifests before
# they're marked ready-to-cache, and to verify them on a future
# /api/verify-bundle route. Deliberately NOT NEXT_PUBLIC_-prefixed: it must
# never reach the client, or anyone could forge a valid bundle signature.
# Not wired into a real signing flow yet — blocked on T12.1 (no live
# Supabase Storage bucket exists). Generate a real value with e.g.
# `openssl rand -hex 32` once that lands.
BUNDLE_SIGNING_SECRET=

# Supabase service-role key (src/lib/supabase/admin.ts) — server-only,
# bypasses Row-Level Security entirely. Used by T19.3's camera_sources
# approve/reject route (src/app/api/camera-sources/[id]/review/route.ts),
# same "no moderator role modeled yet, requires service-role" gap
# 0002_rls.sql/0003_camera_sources.sql document for VERIFIED-promotion and
# camera_sources moderation. Deliberately NOT NEXT_PUBLIC_-prefixed: it must
# never reach the client. Get it from Project Settings > API > service_role
# on a real Supabase project (none exists yet). Also used by the Task 18
# webcam-extraction worker to write MODEL_INFERRED webcam_readings rows,
# which have no insert policy for anon/authenticated by design (see
# supabase/migrations/0005_webcam_readings.sql's RLS section).
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Task 18: Visual Telemetry Extraction Pipeline -------------------------
# See src/lib/webcam-extraction/model.ts for the full founder-cost-flag
# writeup before setting any of these in a real deployment. Short version:
# the Anthropic API has no free tier, so every one of these is a real-money
# lever, not a convenience default.

# Server-only. The vision-model worker (T18.1/T18.2) refuses to call the
# Anthropic API without this — see src/lib/webcam-extraction/vision-client.ts.
# Leave unset until the founder has explicitly confirmed enabling real API
# spend (see WEBCAM_EXTRACTION_ENABLED below).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Explicit founder-confirmation gate (T18.1). Must be the literal string
# "true" to let the worker make any real vision-API call — any other value,
# including unset, means every invocation of
# src/app/api/cron/webcam-extraction/route.ts no-ops (logs and returns,
# calls nothing). This is intentionally NOT implied by ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
# being set — two separate switches, so "a key got added to Vercel env vars"
# doesn't silently start spending money on its own.
WEBCAM_EXTRACTION_ENABLED=

# Shared secret Vercel Cron sends as `Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET` on
# scheduled invocations of the webcam-extraction route; also required for
# the route's manual/dev-trigger path (same route, POST). Leave unset and
# the route refuses every request (fails closed) — see that route's header
# comment for why a missing secret disables the endpoint rather than
# leaving it open. Generate with e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`.
CRON_SECRET=

# Optional override for the T18.5 hard daily call-volume cap
# (src/lib/webcam-extraction/rate-cap.ts). Leave unset to use the
# conservative hardcoded default (DAILY_CALL_CAP, currently 20/day) — only
# set this once real usage patterns justify a different number, and only to
# a small positive integer; an invalid value falls back to the default
# rather than removing the cap.
WEBCAM_EXTRACTION_DAILY_CALL_CAP=

# --- Map-pan AI-assisted discovery fallback (plan.md Resolved Spec --------
# --- Decision #10, 2026-08-11) -------------------------------------------
# Both genuinely free-tier, chosen specifically because Anthropic's/
# OpenAI's hosted web-search tools are metered (no free tier) — see
# src/lib/site-discovery/area-research.ts's header for the full reasoning.
# This is the only feature in the app using either of these two vendors.

# Server-only. Retrieval half of the pipeline (src/lib/site-discovery/
# brave-search.ts). Free tier: 2,000 queries/month, no card required — get
# one at https://brave.com/search/api/. Refuses to call Brave without this
# rather than silently no-opping.
BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY=

# Server-only. Extraction half of the pipeline (src/lib/site-discovery/
# gemini-client.ts) — turns Brave's search results into structured
# candidate dive sites. Free tier, no card required — get one from Google
# AI Studio: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional override for the daily call-volume cap on the combined
# Brave+Gemini pipeline (src/lib/site-discovery/rate-cap.ts). One
# researchDiveSitesNear() call = one Brave search + one Gemini call, so
# this one cap protects both providers' free-tier ceilings at once. Leave
# unset to use the conservative hardcoded default (DAILY_CALL_CAP,
# currently 10/day) — an invalid value falls back to the default rather
# than removing the cap.
AREA_RESEARCH_DAILY_CALL_CAP=
